Alright.

41
00:01:49,220 --> 00:01:50,900
I've gotten lost, but...

42
00:01:51,780 --> 00:01:53,240
I'm busy right now. Later, later.

43
00:01:53,240 --> 00:01:55,860
Ryo-chan, what do you mean you're busy?

44
00:01:55,860 --> 00:01:57,420
Make sure you show him the way properly.

45
00:01:58,540 --> 00:02:00,740
Stop whining and do something about it!

46
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:02,800
Look what you've done, it's ruined!

47
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:04,080
What?

48
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:06,080
Could I borrow a map, please?

49
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,880
Here, go look for it yourself.

50
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:10,780
What year is this map edition from?

51
00:02:11,320 --> 00:02:12,380
How should I know that?

52
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:15,100
It's the latest edition,
published this year.

53
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:16,720
Thanks.

54
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:17,740
No problem.

55
00:02:17,740 --> 00:02:18,900
Officer Nakagawa.

56
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:20,860
I've just returned from patrol.

57
00:02:20,860 --> 00:02:21,960
Good work.

58
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:23,400
I see.

59
00:02:24,080 --> 00:02:26,820
So this river was filled
in and turned into a road.

60
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:28,380
No wonder he got lost.

61
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:31,700
Right, let me convert
the Navicon software first.

62
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:33,460
Navicon?

63
00:02:34,300 --> 00:02:35,580
You have something like that?

64
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:38,640
Yes, could I borrow a
desk for a moment, please?

65
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,640
So it has a computer built in?

66
00:02:49,220 --> 00:02:50,340
Where's the keyboard?

67
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:52,380
An abacus?

68
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:54,360
Looks like it's not just an ordinary abacus.

69
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:56,360
I see.

70
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:03,640
Wow, what amazing finger work.

71
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:13,020
So the abacus is the keyboard?

72
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:17,360
Change complete.

73
00:03:19,220 --> 00:03:19,880
Wow, that's amazing.

74
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:21,360
I'll save it.

75
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:22,960
That's quite something, isn't it.

76
00:03:23,480 --> 00:03:25,480
It's one o'clock. Time for cram school.

77
00:03:26,360 --> 00:03:28,460
Wow, it even manages my schedule.

78
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:31,020
Oh no, I'm going to miss cram school.

79
00:03:31,020 --> 00:03:33,380
I'll at least fax the homework printouts.

80
00:03:34,040 --> 00:03:35,060
If it's a fax,

81
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:36,200
don't you worry.

82
00:03:39,700 --> 00:03:41,580
What? It even has a fax function?

83
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:42,960
It can also be a printer.

84
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:44,980
I can't believe you have
such an amazing backpack.

85
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:46,720
Who exactly are you?

86
00:03:47,180 --> 00:03:48,600
My name is Denkyoku Plus.

87
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:51,600
My father is the president
of Super Denshi Kogi.

88
00:03:53,160 --> 00:03:56,060
It's the most talked-about company

89
00:03:56,440 --> 00:03:57,400
in the electronics field right now.

90
00:03:57,980 --> 00:03:59,980
So you're the rich kid of
such an amazing company.

91
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:03,320
No wonder you have such an incredible thing.

92
00:04:03,320 --> 00:04:06,020
Well, this Super Denshi backpack is

93
00:04:06,020 --> 00:04:07,540
still at the prototype stage,

94
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:09,740
and I'm the one testing it right now.

95
00:04:10,300 --> 00:04:11,980
Does it have other functions too?

96
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:13,800
That's a company secret, but

97
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:17,080
well, as thanks for showing me the map,
I'll show you.

98
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:18,240
Alright, alright.

99
00:04:32,600 --> 00:04:36,360
I film all my classes with
this and print them out.

100
00:04:37,480 --> 00:04:40,820
It's the world's smallest digital camera,
with 48x zoom.

101
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:42,620
Wow!

102
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:46,500
Still, it's a relief to have
something like this in there.

103
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:47,640
How nostalgic.

104
00:04:56,980 --> 00:05:00,040
Here is the weather
forecast for the Tokyo area.

105
00:05:00,560 --> 00:05:02,280
First, the sky conditions.

106
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:06,240
Northerly winds, later southwesterly winds,
becoming somewhat strong.

107
00:05:06,740 --> 00:05:08,760
Don't leave the small stuff to me!

108
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:09,680
Wow, that's cheap!

109
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:13,340
With this whistle,
you can control all electronic devices.

110
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:16,520
Isn't music class going to be tough?

111
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:18,860
with all sorts of switches
getting turned on by accident.

112
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:20,640
since it's still just a prototype.

113
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:23,000
It's pretty heavy

114
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,440
I bet it's at least five kilos.

115
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:26,340
It's for building up the body.

116
00:05:27,220 --> 00:05:29,000
So they've even thought of that?

117
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:31,060
Lend it to me for a sec.

118
00:05:31,060 --> 00:05:32,160
I can't do that.

119
00:05:32,160 --> 00:05:33,360
My father would scold me.

120
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:34,800
Don't be so uptight.

121
00:05:34,800 --> 00:05:36,140
I'll give it right back, I promise.

122
00:05:36,140 --> 00:05:37,700
Ryo-chan, stop it already.

123
00:05:37,700 --> 00:05:39,340
Just a little bit.

124
00:05:42,500 --> 00:05:44,400
My precious flowers...

125
00:05:45,700 --> 00:05:47,180
Ryo-chan.

126
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:55,240


127
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:56,800
This airbag is useless.

128
00:05:57,360 --> 00:05:58,740
It's a fundamental flaw, isn't it?

129
00:06:00,680 --> 00:06:02,620
There's room for improvement.

130
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:04,340
Don't use me as a test subject.

131
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:08,220
Still, this backpack really has everything,
doesn't it?

132
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:10,160
There's an adult version, too.

133
00:06:10,880 --> 00:06:11,720
An adult version?

134
00:06:15,860 --> 00:06:17,660
That's a bit of a creepy thing, isn't it.

135
00:06:18,320 --> 00:06:19,780
What are you thinking?

136
00:06:20,240 --> 00:06:22,260
For adults, it's not a backpack,

137
00:06:22,260 --> 00:06:24,260
it's shaped like an attaché case.

138
00:06:26,800 --> 00:06:27,120
Amazing.

139
00:06:27,620 --> 00:06:29,800
This one even has communication functions

140
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:33,000
If it had a machine gun,
it'd be James Bond, 007.

141
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:36,200
It uses a dedicated
satellite for communication.

142
00:06:36,680 --> 00:06:42,020
Plus, once you register your fingerprint, if anyone other
than the owner carries it, an alarm sounds and it locks up.

143
00:06:42,020 --> 00:06:44,100
Businessmen would probably want that.

144
00:06:44,100 --> 00:06:50,100
It's scheduled to go on sale after the backpack,
and this month we're recruiting monitors for 50,000 yen.

145
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:52,800
50,000 yen? Alright, I'll become one.

146
00:06:52,800 --> 00:06:54,040
Really?

147
00:07:01,820 --> 00:07:04,100
Senpai,
we haven't heard from him at all, have we?

148
00:07:04,520 --> 00:07:07,060
Let's just leave him alone,
Ryo-chan of all people.

149
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:09,380
Senpai!

150
00:07:09,500 --> 00:07:12,480
Hoyoyo.

151
00:07:12,480 --> 00:07:13,900
What's with the hoyoyo?

152
00:07:13,950 --> 00:07:17,520
He took three days off without permission,
and the Chief is furious!

153
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:19,280
What's that supposed to be?

154
00:07:20,060 --> 00:07:23,400
It's his manual. He spent three
days reading through the whole thing.

155
00:07:24,120 --> 00:07:25,860
Outside of work,
he's really diligent, isn't he?

156
00:07:25,860 --> 00:07:34,480
Hey, thanks to that, I've mastered everything from digital camera shooting to using the internet.
I even opened the homepage!

157
00:07:35,660 --> 00:07:43,180
You learned all that in such a short time, that's amazing!
Plus, I begged the president to add some new features.

158
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:48,220
You've really gotten the hang of it, Ryo-chan.
Well, of course!

159
00:07:51,120 --> 00:07:52,460
What's this blinking?

160
00:07:52,460 --> 00:07:54,500
It's the Chief's current location.

161
00:07:55,060 --> 00:07:55,900
The Chief's...

162
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:58,760
I put a transmitter on the Chief.

163
00:07:58,760 --> 00:08:00,240
It's getting closer and closer.

164
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:02,360
That speed means he's in a car.

165
00:08:04,200 --> 00:08:04,780
What is it?

166
00:08:04,780 --> 00:08:07,300
An alarm goes off once
he's within 500 meters.

167
00:08:07,300 --> 00:08:09,820
Whoops, no time to waste on this.

168
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:11,700
I'm going to the monitor.

169
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:12,160
See ya.

170
00:08:12,160 --> 00:08:13,080
Senpai.

171
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:15,780
Ryotsu

172
00:08:15,780 --> 00:08:17,520
He really came, didn't he.

173
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:19,920
Good morning, Chief.

174
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:21,740
Good morning.

175
00:08:22,300 --> 00:08:24,280
Ryotsu had better be here today, for once.

176
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:25,000
Well, that's the thing...

177
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:27,160
What? He's on monitoring duty!

178
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:30,520
That idiot, is he going to
skip the medical checkup again?

179
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,100
Medical checkup?

180
00:08:32,320 --> 00:08:33,458
That Ryotsu...

181
00:08:33,508 --> 00:08:36,480
he hasn't had a regular
checkup in fifteen years!

182
00:08:37,260 --> 00:08:37,980
That bad?

183
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:41,800
This morning, the station chief lectured me
again about a complaint on my supervision.

184
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:47,500
I just told him I'd stake my job on
getting him to take a medical checkup.

185
00:08:49,180 --> 00:08:50,760
You don't have to go that far.

186
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:52,680
Anyway, find Ryotsu.

187
00:08:52,680 --> 00:08:54,020
That's impossible.

188
00:08:54,020 --> 00:08:55,920
He's like a bullet out of a gun, sir.

189
00:08:57,020 --> 00:08:58,860
Isn't there some way to track him down?

190
00:08:59,240 --> 00:09:00,820
At this rate, my job is on the line.

191
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:02,000
That's right.

192
00:09:02,380 --> 00:09:03,700
Let's call Plus-kun.

193
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:09,820
Step right up, step right up!

194
00:09:09,820 --> 00:09:11,940
The movie now showing in theaters

195
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:13,380
can be watched right away, just like that!

196
00:09:14,060 --> 00:09:15,900
And to top it off,
it's only 1,000 yen a piece!

197
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:17,400
Come on, we're winning, we're winning!

198
00:09:18,220 --> 00:09:20,120
Eighth one! Eighth one! Eighth one!

199
00:09:20,640 --> 00:09:21,500
Eighth one!

200
00:09:21,820 --> 00:09:22,520
Eighth one!

201
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:47,520
Eighth one!

202
00:09:48,540 --> 00:09:49,880
Hurry up and get back here!

203
00:09:49,880 --> 00:09:51,520
Ugh, you're so annoying.

204
00:09:54,960 --> 00:09:56,320
Hang up the phone already.

205
00:09:56,880 --> 00:10:00,620
Plus-kun, is there no other
way to track that guy down?

206
00:10:00,620 --> 00:10:04,640
Didn't he say he attached
a transmitter to the Chief?

207
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:07,560
I think we can trace it
back using the frequency.

208
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:09,760
Alright, let's search for the transmitter.

209
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:12,320
It should be somewhere on the Chief's body.

210
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:14,840
Honestly, when did he even do that?

211
00:10:14,840 --> 00:10:17,520
Alright, where is it,
where is it, where is it?

212
00:10:21,180 --> 00:10:23,180
No, sorry, my bad.

213
00:10:23,560 --> 00:10:24,440
N-no, sir.

214
00:10:25,300 --> 00:10:28,040
Isn't there some other way to make money?

215
00:10:28,040 --> 00:10:29,120
You're fired.

216
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:31,240
Sorry, Chief.

217
00:10:31,900 --> 00:10:33,160
What do you think you're doing?

218
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:34,460
Please, anything but that.

219
00:10:34,460 --> 00:10:35,300
It's not me, is it?

220
00:10:35,700 --> 00:10:37,700
You'll lose hundreds of millions in profits!

221
00:10:38,520 --> 00:10:39,240
Hundreds of millions?

222
00:10:40,460 --> 00:10:41,560
Hey, what's going on?

223
00:10:41,920 --> 00:10:44,380
The computer installed
in the car broke down,

224
00:10:44,980 --> 00:10:48,140
and now we can't get important information.

225
00:10:49,220 --> 00:10:50,467
If it's a PC communication,

226
00:10:50,517 --> 00:10:53,400
my Super Electronic GX767 can handle it.

227
00:10:53,640 --> 00:10:54,460
Really?

228
00:10:59,660 --> 00:11:02,840
But the access fee is steep.

229
00:11:03,420 --> 00:11:07,260
Since it looks like you'll make a killing,
I'll take 10% of the profits.

230
00:11:07,940 --> 00:11:10,020
That's too much. One percent.

231
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:13,280
Fine. How about we meet in the middle at 7%?

232
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:14,680
Where's the middle?

233
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:16,640
If you don't like it, that's fine.

234
00:11:17,240 --> 00:11:20,620
Okay, okay, 7%. Let's shake on it.

235
00:11:20,620 --> 00:11:22,360
Alright, the deal's done.

236
00:11:23,580 --> 00:11:25,380
Hurry, it's the White House!

237
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:27,520
Exactly at 5 p.m. Japan time,

238
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:30,480
the next year's Orange Safe
buyback price will be announced.

239
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:31,400
That's what I want to know.

240
00:11:32,100 --> 00:11:34,400
We don't have time! Where's the address?

241
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:35,340
Here it is.

242
00:11:35,780 --> 00:11:36,720
The password is...

243
00:11:37,660 --> 00:11:38,180
Okay, there we go.

244
00:11:41,660 --> 00:11:42,740
That's awfully fast.

245
00:11:42,740 --> 00:11:45,120
It's because they're using a
dedicated communications satellite.

246
00:11:46,640 --> 00:11:47,800
The Orange price has come up!

247
00:11:48,220 --> 00:11:49,180
It's higher than last year.

248
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:53,720
Hey, contact headquarters and buy up all
the orange-related stocks in the world.

249
00:11:53,720 --> 00:11:54,160
Yes, sir.

250
00:11:58,580 --> 00:12:00,340
Sorry, my battery's dead.

251
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:01,500
You idiot!

252
00:12:01,880 --> 00:12:03,380
Use my phone.

253
00:12:03,380 --> 00:12:05,580
It's a dedicated line,
so it'll connect right away.

254
00:12:05,580 --> 00:12:06,980
Thanks!

255
00:12:09,220 --> 00:12:09,860
Found it!

256
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:12,560
That guy, and he's the one who
should be paying the bonuses.

257
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:15,080
Give it here, I'll connect it right away.

258
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:20,620
I'll find him and make him get that medical checkup,
no matter what.

259
00:12:34,080 --> 00:12:38,680
Wow, the stock of the Singapore mayor's
orange-related company just doubled!

260
00:12:39,600 --> 00:12:41,460
Yes, yes, Mr. Ryotsu!

261
00:12:41,900 --> 00:12:44,960
The London stock market
should open any moment now.

262
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:47,380
Got it.

263
00:12:48,100 --> 00:12:48,960
Here it comes, here it comes!

264
00:12:48,960 --> 00:12:50,780
Where are the orange stocks?

265
00:12:50,780 --> 00:12:52,280
As soon as trading begins...

266
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:53,460
London is up twofold!

267
00:12:54,060 --> 00:12:55,040
Good, sell out now!

268
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:57,660
Idiot, how could you ever compete with Nizō?

269
00:12:58,380 --> 00:13:01,000
Stocks are stocks,
but it's not like oicho gambling, you know.

270
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:02,340
It's pretty much the same thing.

271
00:13:02,680 --> 00:13:04,900
Wait, wait, hold on until it triples!

272
00:13:05,360 --> 00:13:06,920
There's no way it'll go that far.

273
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:14,760
But this is quite lavish, isn't it.

274
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:18,040
I made about 300 million yen. Thanks.

275
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:20,620
300 million yen Well, that's great.

276
00:13:20,900 --> 00:13:22,740
No, no. It's 300 million dollars.

277
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:26,260
Dollars, even at 110 yen to the dollar

278
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:28,560
33 billion yen!?

279
00:13:28,560 --> 00:13:29,923
Yes. Now then,

280
00:13:29,973 --> 00:13:32,800
here's your cut. It's 7%, right?

281
00:13:33,380 --> 00:13:36,350
1, 10, 12,

282
00:13:36,400 --> 00:13:39,420
2.31 billion yen!?

283
00:13:40,540 --> 00:13:42,780
2.31 billion yen!

284
00:13:44,240 --> 00:13:45,860
Is it really okay for me to get this much?

285
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:48,460
Yes, we had an agreement, remember?

286
00:13:48,460 --> 00:13:51,280
Besides, you have a talent for business.

287
00:13:51,700 --> 00:13:54,020
Won't you become my partner?

288
00:13:54,020 --> 00:13:55,420
Partner

289
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:58,880
Become my co-owner for an
annual salary of 1 billion yen.

290
00:13:59,720 --> 00:14:00,840
1 billion yen

291
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:02,800
Full amount!

292
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:04,360
No, no, no, no.

293
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:06,040
Okay, okay.

294
00:14:22,340 --> 00:14:23,240
Good morning.

295
00:14:24,140 --> 00:14:25,140
Morning.

296
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:32,220
Good morning.

297
00:14:32,220 --> 00:14:34,900
Good morning.

298
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:41,540
How does the vice president's chair feel?

299
00:14:41,540 --> 00:14:42,920
Not bad.

300
00:14:43,960 --> 00:14:46,680
This is terrible!
A disaster has struck Ukraine,

301
00:14:46,730 --> 00:14:49,040
and the wheat has been devastated, they say.

302
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:49,600
What?

303
00:14:52,380 --> 00:14:54,760
The American wheat market is soaring.

304
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:59,380
Have other investors already
cornered the American wheat?

305
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:02,400
Corner the Australian wheat!

306
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:04,260
Hold on, a phone call won't do.

307
00:15:04,680 --> 00:15:06,660
At times like this,
you need the physical stock in hand.

308
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:09,440
Negotiating directly with the
farm owners is the best way.

309
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:10,600
I see.

310
00:15:11,820 --> 00:15:12,440
Vice President.

311
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:15,660
Will you fly to Australia with me?

312
00:15:16,100 --> 00:15:17,160
That's my own theory, you know.

313
00:15:17,920 --> 00:15:19,800
I've had a direct flight
standing by at Haneda.

314
00:15:20,140 --> 00:15:21,680
We'll fly nonstop all
the way there with this.

315
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:23,840
Executives really are different

316
00:15:27,480 --> 00:15:30,080
Ryo-san seems to have
headed for Haneda Airport.

317
00:15:30,080 --> 00:15:33,020
Ryo-chan must be planning
to skip town somewhere.

318
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:34,920
Hokkaido or Kyushu?

319
00:15:34,920 --> 00:15:35,780
I wonder.

320
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:40,760
That plane.

321
00:15:42,580 --> 00:15:43,520
Overseas, then?

322
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:54,760
Chief, what are you going to do?

323
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:56,840
My neck is on the line here.

324
00:15:56,840 --> 00:15:59,740
No matter what,
I'm making him get that medical checkup.

325
00:16:00,240 --> 00:16:01,120
He's not getting away.

326
00:16:01,120 --> 00:16:02,200
Lear Jet.

327
00:16:02,200 --> 00:16:03,080
Chief.

328
00:16:03,080 --> 00:16:05,680
Leave the plane arrangements to me.

329
00:16:09,880 --> 00:16:12,600
With this FR-71, we'll definitely catch up.

330
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:30,640
He's tougher than I thought.

331
00:16:30,640 --> 00:16:31,880
That old fox.

332
00:16:32,720 --> 00:16:34,120
Ugh, of all times to call!

333
00:16:35,280 --> 00:16:35,940
Hello?

334
00:16:35,940 --> 00:16:36,980
Ryotsu!

335
00:16:36,980 --> 00:16:40,040
What are you doing all
the way out in Australia?

336
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,980
Chief, how did you find me here?

337
00:16:41,980 --> 00:16:45,000
Ryo-san, going all the way
overseas to keep an eye on things?

338
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:46,340
I never asked you to.

339
00:16:47,180 --> 00:16:48,180
What's wrong?

340
00:16:48,720 --> 00:16:49,620
Nothing.

341
00:16:49,620 --> 00:16:52,540
And I'm in the middle of
an important business deal!

342
00:16:57,680 --> 00:16:58,320
Whoa!

343
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:03,940
Ryo-san, come out!

344
00:17:03,940 --> 00:17:06,920
Go straight back to Japan
and get a medical checkup!

345
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:08,600
Grrr...

346
00:17:09,100 --> 00:17:11,100
Chief, what on earth is that?

347
00:17:11,100 --> 00:17:13,080
Damn that Nakagawa!

348
00:17:13,500 --> 00:17:14,940
I'm not getting caught here.

349
00:17:14,940 --> 00:17:16,720
Let's wrap up the deal quickly.

350
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:19,140
Ugh, they're bringing it already,
aren't they?

351
00:17:23,660 --> 00:17:25,420
What a wonderful decision.

352
00:17:26,500 --> 00:17:29,880
Eeeh! Can't this thing go any faster?!

353
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:31,760
Not any further!

354
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:34,620
It was sheer guts! Pure guts!

355
00:17:34,860 --> 00:17:38,540
Ryotsu!
No matter where you run, you can't escape!

356
00:17:38,940 --> 00:17:41,560
We've got the Super Randoseru on our side,
so don't forget it!

357
00:17:42,460 --> 00:17:46,060
We've got our own Super Me too!

358
00:17:46,700 --> 00:17:47,720
It's Mr. Maria!

359
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:51,480
So come back with me and
get your medical checkup!

360
00:17:52,020 --> 00:17:53,889
I quit being a cop and

361
00:17:53,939 --> 00:17:57,080
I became vice president with a
salary of 1 billion yen a year!

362
00:17:57,980 --> 00:18:01,180
I'm not getting a police
medical checkup now!

363
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:03,880
What are you babbling about?!

364
00:18:04,300 --> 00:18:07,680
We're in completely different worlds
from an ordinary chief like you now!

365
00:18:08,180 --> 00:18:09,040
Goodbye!

366
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:13,560
What do you mean, goodbye!

367
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:16,300
Nakagawa, can't you use a warning shot?

368
00:18:16,520 --> 00:18:18,220
We're not armed or anything!

369
00:18:18,540 --> 00:18:20,040
Ryotsu, don't you have anything?

370
00:18:21,480 --> 00:18:22,180
It has something attached, though.

371
00:18:23,800 --> 00:18:25,220
It even has something like that on it?

372
00:18:25,220 --> 00:18:26,500
Of course you can trust it.

373
00:18:27,160 --> 00:18:28,440
Good, that's enough.

374
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,720
You're so persistent!

375
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:34,100
Nice work, Plus-kun.

376
00:18:35,440 --> 00:18:36,660
What are you planning to do?

377
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,360
Here I go!

378
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:44,280
What's going on here?

379
00:18:44,280 --> 00:18:46,220
If that's how you want it,

380
00:18:46,220 --> 00:18:48,260
There's a missile attached to the randoseru!

381
00:18:48,600 --> 00:18:50,760
Even if it's a death sentence,
there should be weapons on it.

382
00:18:51,480 --> 00:18:52,080
Found it, found it!

383
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:53,880
All right!

384
00:19:02,080 --> 00:19:03,040
Alright!

385
00:19:03,840 --> 00:19:05,140
Here we go!

386
00:19:06,060 --> 00:19:06,800
Hahaha!

387
00:19:06,980 --> 00:19:08,140
You dug your own grave!

388
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:11,100
Nakagawa, deport him straight back to Japan!

389
00:19:11,140 --> 00:19:11,640
Roger!

390
00:19:15,740 --> 00:19:16,480
Alright!

391
00:19:16,480 --> 00:19:16,740
Yikes!

392
00:19:17,420 --> 00:19:18,600
Aaah!

393
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:22,240
What's this button?

394
00:19:24,300 --> 00:19:24,920
Whoa!

395
00:19:26,220 --> 00:19:27,360
Whoa!

396
00:19:28,540 --> 00:19:29,300
Yocchan!

397
00:19:29,860 --> 00:19:33,560
Whoa!

398
00:19:38,300 --> 00:19:41,340
Hahahaha! Justice always wins!

399
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:43,240
It's ah-ah-ah!

400
00:19:43,240 --> 00:19:45,420
Grr! You lucky bastard!

401
00:19:46,480 --> 00:19:49,560
Hey, isn't there some other
good way to catch Ryo-chan?

402
00:19:49,880 --> 00:19:52,760
I can track him, but catching him is...

403
00:19:53,160 --> 00:19:55,480
Why don't we call him again
and try to persuade him?

404
00:19:55,900 --> 00:19:56,560
It's useless.

405
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:59,380
Wait, I have a good idea.

406
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:08,160
Hey, hey, this isn't a show!

407
00:20:10,780 --> 00:20:12,940
Hey, buddy, it's here, it's here!

408
00:20:13,800 --> 00:20:16,180
Yo, this is no time for that!

409
00:20:16,180 --> 00:20:18,080
The gold price is falling.

410
00:20:18,520 --> 00:20:21,480
Sell all the gold our
company holds right away.

411
00:20:22,020 --> 00:20:22,680
Got it.

412
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,140
Hurry up, you hear?

413
00:20:25,140 --> 00:20:26,340
No need to panic.

414
00:20:27,400 --> 00:20:29,700
That's strange. I can't access it.

415
00:20:30,300 --> 00:20:33,700
What are you doing? Hurry,
or our company will suffer huge losses!

416
00:20:34,180 --> 00:20:36,900
Even so, that's odd.

417
00:20:37,760 --> 00:20:41,780
We're losing 50 million
dollars every second!

418
00:20:42,940 --> 00:20:43,780
Hurry up, Ryotsu!

419
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:45,000
I know.

420
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:47,380
So the fax was receiving?

421
00:20:47,380 --> 00:20:48,960
No wonder we couldn't get through.

422
00:20:49,980 --> 00:20:52,360
Who's sending this in an emergency?

423
00:20:53,260 --> 00:20:54,160
The Chief?

424
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:57,140
Ryotsu, what are you doing?

425
00:20:57,580 --> 00:20:59,620
At this rate, our company is going bankrupt.

426
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:02,440
I'll stop the fax right now.

427
00:21:03,060 --> 00:21:04,640
The switch is inside.

428
00:21:06,160 --> 00:21:06,800
Look at that!

429
00:21:07,700 --> 00:21:08,980
It's locked up.

430
00:21:10,040 --> 00:21:12,880
We're already $1.02
billion in the red, Ryotsu!

431
00:21:12,940 --> 00:21:14,500
A voice lock

432
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:16,760
We have no choice but to open it from above.

433
00:21:16,760 --> 00:21:19,160
Wasn't it do-mi-so?

434
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:27,340
Maybe it was do-fa-la?

435
00:21:32,140 --> 00:21:32,840
Aaaaaah!

436
00:21:35,740 --> 00:21:36,580
Aaaaaah!

437
00:21:37,620 --> 00:21:38,460
Eeeeeeh!

438
00:21:44,860 --> 00:21:46,160
What's all the noise? Shut up!

439
00:21:46,600 --> 00:21:48,840
Two chuka-don and one ramen rice, got it?

440
00:21:48,840 --> 00:21:49,980
Don't mess around!

441
00:21:51,860 --> 00:21:52,780
If it breaks, we're in trouble.

442
00:21:54,440 --> 00:21:54,820
I see.

443
00:21:55,220 --> 00:21:55,600
I see.

444
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:58,440
What are you doing?

445
00:21:58,440 --> 00:22:00,080
Sell the gold, quick!

446
00:22:00,080 --> 00:22:01,300
I know, I know.

447
00:22:02,340 --> 00:22:04,080
Thief! Thief!

448
00:22:04,300 --> 00:22:05,980
Hey, I'm the real one, hey!

449
00:22:06,200 --> 00:22:07,800
Thief! Thief!

450
00:22:07,860 --> 00:22:09,780
Ow ow! Stop it, let go!

451
00:22:09,960 --> 00:22:11,520
It's me, Ryotsu, the owner!

452
00:22:11,520 --> 00:22:13,140
Fingerprints confirmed as
not belonging to the owner.

453
00:22:13,140 --> 00:22:14,700
I'm telling you, I'm the real owner!

454
00:22:15,260 --> 00:22:16,140
Ryotsu!

455
00:22:17,580 --> 00:22:20,700
To protect the secret data,
it will explode in 60 seconds.

456
00:22:21,260 --> 00:22:21,820
What!?

457
00:22:23,020 --> 00:22:23,420
58

458
00:22:23,420 --> 00:22:24,600
Don't mess with me!

459
00:22:24,820 --> 00:22:26,900
Ugh, Ryotsu, you bastard!

460
00:22:27,320 --> 00:22:28,480
This is no time for that!

461
00:22:28,700 --> 00:22:31,700
At this rate, we're going down with it!

462
00:22:32,020 --> 00:22:33,160
50 seconds left.

463
00:22:34,280 --> 00:22:35,680
Mr. Ryotsu,

464
00:22:35,730 --> 00:22:39,760
you have quite a unique knack for business,
don't you?

465
00:22:39,760 --> 00:22:43,420
W-really? I always suspected as much.

466
00:22:43,420 --> 00:22:46,740
Not bad for me to see
through it at a glance, is it?

467
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:49,040
But

468
00:22:49,860 --> 00:22:51,040
My hunches...

469
00:22:52,300 --> 00:22:54,140
Looks like my eyes were
nothing but knotholes.

470
00:22:54,140 --> 00:22:55,840
You're fired.

471
00:22:59,460 --> 00:23:02,900
I'll use this to cover
the losses you caused.

472
00:23:04,100 --> 00:23:04,460
3

473
00:23:04,980 --> 00:23:05,340
2

474
00:23:05,900 --> 00:23:06,260
1

475
00:23:13,040 --> 00:23:15,860
Looks like the secret data
protection device has activated.

476
00:23:26,840 --> 00:23:30,420
Surviving that explosion...
what a lucky bastard he is.

477
00:23:30,420 --> 00:23:35,100
There was less explosive, and the
safety airbag went off too, didn't it?

478
00:23:35,640 --> 00:23:38,280
I'll report to my father
that this needs improving.

479
00:23:38,720 --> 00:23:42,240
I'll take a checkup or anything else,
so please help me!

480
00:23:43,320 --> 00:23:45,540
Didn't Ryotsu quit the police?

481
00:23:46,020 --> 00:23:47,200
You don't have to take it anymore.

482
00:23:47,740 --> 00:23:49,060
Thank you for being our test subject.

483
00:23:50,100 --> 00:23:52,060
I'll transfer your pay to your bank account.

484
00:23:52,060 --> 00:23:53,700
Alright, everyone, let's go home.

485
00:23:53,700 --> 00:23:54,560
Yeah, yeah.

486
00:23:56,020 --> 00:23:59,000
Wait, please! That was just a joke!

487
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:01,600
That's too cold, as a human being.

488
00:24:04,040 --> 00:24:06,020
What? You don't approve of the marriage?

489
00:24:06,020 --> 00:24:08,580
Chief, what are you thinking?

490
00:24:08,580 --> 00:24:11,480
Please at least think
about how Hiromi-san feels.

491
00:24:11,480 --> 00:24:12,340
As a parent,

492
00:24:12,340 --> 00:24:14,820
Fine. If you're going to take that attitude,

493
00:24:14,820 --> 00:24:17,580
we'll hold the wedding ourselves.
Understood?

494
00:24:17,580 --> 00:24:21,220
Here we go! Assembly! Even the
Chief's eyes are welling up! Good luck!

495
00:24:48,540 --> 00:24:57,960
Even if it's raining today,

496
00:24:57,960 --> 00:25:03,480
tomorrow the sun will shine.

497
00:25:03,480 --> 00:25:08,620
Bye-bye, let's wave goodbye.

498
00:25:08,620 --> 00:25:13,900
Unpleasant things, farewell.

499
00:25:13,900 --> 00:25:21,480
Oh yeah, let's try living however we like.

500
00:25:21,480 --> 00:25:23,980
Good things will come.

501
00:25:23,980 --> 00:25:30,280
The sun is calling you
from outside the door.

502
00:25:43,900 --> 00:25:44,000
Thank you for watching.

